course: dictionary
lesson: 15045
title: Quick, sharp replies
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A retort is a quick, sharp answer, often given back to someone who has just said something rude or unfair. As a verb, to retort means to answer in that quick, sharp way.
explain: Writers use retorted instead of said when the reply is fast and cheeky. «"Not likely!" she retorted.» The word tells you that her answer was quick and a little angry, not just spoken calmly.
explain: Look at the words around retort for clues. «"You can't catch me!" he retorted angrily.» The word angrily shows the feeling. «Her witty retort made everyone laugh» uses retort as a noun, meaning the clever reply itself.
fact: Retort (verb) means to answer quickly and sharply, often angrily or cleverly.
fact: «"Not likely!" she retorted.» Retorted is used instead of said for a quick, cheeky reply.
fact: Retort (noun) means a quick, sharp or clever reply, as in «a witty retort».
fact: Phrases to know: «retorted angrily» and «a witty retort».
fact: An old science meaning is a glass container with a long bent neck, used for heating and distilling liquids. Pictures of old laboratories show retorts.
exercise: «"Fine, then, do it yourself!" Tom retorted.» What does retorted mean here? | Cried with happiness | Whispered very softly | Forgot to speak | *Answered quickly and sharply
exercise: Lily had a witty retort ready for the teacher. What is a retort in this sentence? | A long, sleepy yawn | A pair of spectacles | *A quick, clever reply | A map of the town
exercise: The old professor placed a glass retort on the bench. What is a retort in this sentence? | A quick, cheeky reply | *A glass container with a long bent neck | A small, furry animal | A type of bread
test: «"You're wrong!" Maya retorted angrily.» Which word shows how Maya spoke? | Maya | You're | Wrong | *Angrily
test: «Dad's retort made us all laugh.» What does retort mean in this sentence? | A sleepy yawn | A type of glass jar used in old labs | *A quick, sharp reply | A long journey
exam: In «She gave a retort that surprised everyone», what does retort mean? | A loud noise in the street | A glass container for heating liquids | A slow, quiet goodbye | *A quick, sharp reply
